---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildWebAppSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';
import { BOOK_AVAILABLE, BOOK_PRICE } from '../../../config';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../../lib/schema';

const appSchema = buildWebAppSchema({
  name: "Stencil Creator",
  description: "Turn any photo into a print-ready multi-layer cut stencil and export as PNG, PDF or cut-ready SVG. Runs in the browser, no signup.",
  path: "/tools/stencil-creator/",
  free: true,
});
const crumbSchema = buildBreadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Tools', path: '/tools/' }, { name: 'Stencil Creator' }]);

---
<BaseLayout
  title="Stencil Creator — Photo to Cut-Ready Stencil | AirbrushDOC"
  description="Free browser tool that turns any photo into a print-ready, multi-layer cut stencil. Export PNG, PDF or cut-ready SVG, one file per layer. No signup, nothing to install."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(crumbSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(appSchema)} />
  <main class="abd-container">
    <div class="blg-page-header" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <nav class="blg-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="blg-breadcrumbs-sep">›</span>
        <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
        <span class="blg-breadcrumbs-sep">›</span>
        <span>Stencil Creator</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="blg-title-row">
        <h1 class="blg-page-title">Stencil <span class="blg-page-title-accent">Creator</span></h1>
      </div>
      <p class="sc-lede">
        Turn a photo into a print-ready, multi-layer cut stencil. Import an image, set your layers
        and thresholds, then export as PNG, print-ready PDF, or cut-ready SVG, one file per layer.
        It runs entirely in your browser, free, with no signup and nothing to install.
      </p>
      <div class="blg-header-line" style="margin-top: 16px;"></div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <div class="sc-frame-wrap">
    <iframe
      src="/tools/stencil-creator.html"
      title="Stencil Creator — photo to multi-layer cut stencil"
      class="sc-frame"
      allowfullscreen
    ></iframe>
  </div>

  <main class="abd-container">
    <section class="tool-about">
      <h2>Making airbrush stencils by hand</h2>
      <p>You do not need software to cut a usable stencil. Print the image at final size, trace it
      onto low-tack frisket film or thin acetate, and cut with a fresh blade on a self-healing mat.
      The two things that decide whether it works are bridges, the small uncut links that stop
      islands falling out, and how well the film seals at the edge. A stencil that lifts even
      slightly will let paint creep underneath and blur every edge on the piece.</p>
      <p>Multi-layer stencils are the same idea repeated. Each layer covers one tonal band, sprayed
      lightest to darkest, with registration marks so the layers line up. That is the part that gets
      tedious by hand, and it is the part the Stencil Creator automates: it splits a photo into
      layers by luminosity and exports one cut file per layer.</p>
      <p>The SVG export is cut-ready, so it goes straight to a vinyl cutter or craft cutting machine
      as well as to a blade and a mat.</p>
      <p class="tool-about-next"><strong>Free stencils and guides:</strong>
        <a href="/blog/multi-layer-stencils/">Multi-layer stencils</a> ·
        <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-stencil-in-coreldraw/">Make a stencil in CorelDRAW</a> ·
        <a href="/freebies/">Free stencil packs</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="sc-book">
      <div class="sc-book-text">
        <h2 class="sc-book-title">Cutting the stencil is the easy half</h2>
        <p>What decides the result is everything after: how you seal the edge, the order you spray
        the layers in, and the pressure and thinning that stop paint creeping underneath.
        <em>The Airbrush Technique Bible</em> is the manual for that part, and it ships with an
        offline copy of this tool so it keeps working with no internet.</p>
        {BOOK_AVAILABLE
          ? <a href="/book/" class="abd-btn-primary">Get the book — {BOOK_PRICE} →</a>
          : <a href="/book/" class="abd-btn-primary">Read the free preview →</a>}
        {!BOOK_AVAILABLE && <p class="sc-book-note">In final editing. Subscribe on the book page and you will get the launch email.</p>}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.sc-lede {
  max-width: 68ch;
  margin: 14px 0 0;
  color: var(--abd-text-dim);
  line-height: 1.7;
  font-size: 0.98rem;
}

.sc-frame-wrap {
  width: 100%;
  height: calc(100vh - 260px);
  min-height: 620px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--abd-border);
}
.sc-frame {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  border: none;
  display: block;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .sc-frame-wrap {
    height: calc(100vh - 200px);
    min-height: 540px;
  }
}

.tool-about {
  max-width: 68ch;
  margin: 48px auto 0;
  padding: 28px 0 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--abd-border, #2a2a2a);
  text-align: left;
}
.tool-about h2 { font-family: var(--abd-font-display); font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 14px; }
.tool-about p { color: var(--abd-text-dim); line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 14px; }
.tool-about-next { margin-top: 18px; }

.sc-book {
  max-width: 68ch;
  margin: 40px auto 72px;
  padding: 26px 24px;
  border: 1px solid var(--abd-border, #2a2a2a);
  border-radius: 6px;
}
.sc-book-title {
  font-family: var(--abd-font-display);
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  margin: 0 0 12px;
}
.sc-book p {
  color: var(--abd-text-dim);
  line-height: 1.75;
  margin: 0 0 18px;
}
.sc-book-note {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  color: var(--abd-text-muted);
  margin: 14px 0 0;
}
</style>
